{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/750519-do-beasts-regain-willpower-by-sleeping","id":750519,"title":"Do Beasts regain Willpower by sleeping?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-02T19:59:40-08:00","id":750519,"title":"Do Beasts regain Willpower by sleeping?","content":"I can't find this anywhere. If they don't, I feel like it would be beneficial to explicitly point this out, as it is a common expectation for those that have played other nWOD games in the past.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think I found something. Page 236, when talking about what changes when becoming Unfettered: As the Unfettered<br /> don\u2019t need to sleep, they do not refresh Willpower through rest.<br /> <br /> Seems to imply that Beasts do regain willpower from sleeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-02-2015, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T03:55:59-08:00","id":751068,"title":"","content":"In general, all supernaturals follow the rules of the base mortals unless something in their books tell them not to. VtR specifically says, at one point, that vampires do not regain willpower with sleep. The Beast pdf doesn't seem to say anywhere that you don't regain willpower from sleep. Ergo, you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:47:40-08:00","id":751314,"title":"","content":"Well, actually VtR doesn't. It was supposed to, but they neglected to make it explicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:36:57-08:00","id":751584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/750519-do-beasts-regain-willpower-by-sleeping?p=751314#post751314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually VtR doesn't. It was supposed to, but they neglected to make it explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. VTR also has a line about Strix not needing to sleep, and therefore not regaining willpower through it. Sounds kind of like the line about the Unfettered, right?<br /> This kind of stuff really needs to be explicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T23:03:02-08:00","id":773672,"title":"","content":"The more I think about this, the more it bothers me. The second edition books are supposed to completely contain all of the rules required to play the new splat - that's why they have combat chapters, all of the conditions and merits, etc.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mention that Beasts regain willpower through sleep anywhere. But some places kind of imply they should. But some places in B&amp;S did the same.<br /> <br /> There are similar oversights throughout all of the second edition books, and I can't help but wonder if these things are being playtested enough. GMC, Vampire, Werewolf, Demon, and Beast all contain references to a Condition that doesn't exist (Vulnerable), for example.<br /> <br /> VTR and Beast both neglect to mention willpower via sleeping, despite implying it should be a thing (even though it explicitly isn't in Vampire per Word of God). Werewolf doesn't mention it. Neither does Demon, but Demon DOES refer the player to the WOD core rulebook for rules on Willpower, so I suppose they explicitly recover it via sleep.<br /> <br /> Since none of the self-contained second edition games contain any references to regaining willpower during sleep, and since one of them has been said to explicitly not, I guess the only reasonable conclusion is that none of them do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}